WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:04.870
There's a new Valkyrie in the pages of Marvel
comics - and her face is a familiar one.

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:08.120
"You're far more clever than anyone else in
this realm."

00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:09.560
"Realm?

00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:10.920
Realm?"

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:14.280
The House of Ideas has confirmed that none
other than Jane Foster will return from her

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:19.310
apparent death to take on the mantle in her
own series, Jane Foster: Valkyrie.

00:00:19.310 --> 00:00:22.150
The first issue is slated for publication
in July.

00:00:22.150 --> 00:00:26.820
The move comes in the aftermath of the massive
Marvel crossover event War of the Realms,

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:31.540
which saw the Dark Elf Malekith the Accursed
mounting a conquest of all ten realms.

00:00:31.540 --> 00:00:36.879
With only Midgard (aka Earth) left standing,
a massive roster of Marvel's heroes assembled

00:00:36.879 --> 00:00:41.570
to combat the threat, including, of course,
Thor and Loki, who were key to thwarting Malekith's

00:00:41.570 --> 00:00:42.600
plot.

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:46.450
The well-received event featured such standout
moments as Wolverine coming to the rescue

00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:51.409
of the Punisher, Ghost Rider teaming up with
Doctor Strange, and Daredevil briefly attaining

00:00:51.409 --> 00:00:53.089
godlike power.

00:00:53.089 --> 00:00:57.289
Of course, it wouldn't be a Mighty Marvel
crossover without a few casualties, and War

00:00:57.289 --> 00:00:59.420
of the Realms was no exception.

00:00:59.420 --> 00:01:04.719
Among the most notable: Brunnhilde the Valkyrie,
who in issue #2 of the main series was decapitated

00:01:04.719 --> 00:01:06.280
by Malekith himself.

00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:10.610
With the valiant warrior gone, the door was
open for a new Valkyrie to emerge, and Foster

00:01:10.610 --> 00:01:12.430
should fit the bill nicely.

00:01:12.430 --> 00:01:16.750
The character has a long history in the comics,
having first appeared in Journey into Mystery

00:01:16.750 --> 00:01:21.950
#84 in 1962 - before Thor even had his own
solo title.

00:01:21.950 --> 00:01:26.280
Although she primarily served as a love interest
for the God of Thunder for much of her publication

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:30.850
history, the character has become much more
prominent in Marvel lore in recent years.

00:01:30.850 --> 00:01:36.350
Following her portrayal onscreen by Natalie
Portman in 2011's Thor and 2013's Thor: The

00:01:36.350 --> 00:01:41.710
Dark World, Marvel decided that it was time
for her to take the spotlight - and in 2014,

00:01:41.710 --> 00:01:44.560
she did just that, in dramatic fashion.

00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:49.030
In a storyline in Thor's solo book that year,
Foster was diagnosed with breast cancer at

00:01:49.030 --> 00:01:53.249
around the same time that Thor lost the ability
to wield Mjolnir during a battle with Nick

00:01:53.249 --> 00:01:54.249
Fury.

00:01:54.249 --> 00:01:58.430
The mighty weapon, abandoned on the Moon,
telepathically called out to Foster - who,

00:01:58.430 --> 00:02:02.189
with the aid of Heimdall, retrieved it and
became the first woman to harness the power

00:02:02.189 --> 00:02:03.560
of Thor.

00:02:03.560 --> 00:02:07.639
Foster held down the mantle for a number of
years, but unfortunately, each transformation

00:02:07.639 --> 00:02:12.040
into Thor resulted in her cancer progressing
at an accelerated rate.

00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:16.160
She eventually succumbed to the disease after
a brutal battle with Mangog, the physical

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:20.090
manifestation of the collective hatred of
a race which was slaughtered by the armies

00:02:20.090 --> 00:02:25.080
of Asgard in centuries past - but she was
revived by Odin in recognition of her valiant

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:27.310
efforts against the forces of evil.

00:02:27.310 --> 00:02:31.959
She then convinced Thor to reclaim his title,
focusing her energies on battling the disease

00:02:31.959 --> 00:02:33.780
which still threatened her life.

00:02:33.780 --> 00:02:38.250
Given her experience wielding the power of
Asgard's mightiest warrior, Foster is a brilliant

00:02:38.250 --> 00:02:40.840
choice to take on the mantle of Valkyrie.

00:02:40.840 --> 00:02:45.489
Marvel's publication arm seems to increasingly
be taking its cues from the outrageously successful

00:02:45.489 --> 00:02:50.050
Marvel Cinematic Universe, a trend illustrated
by this latest move.

00:02:50.050 --> 00:02:54.470
It's safe to say that Jane Foster's name recognition
skyrocketed thanks to her inclusion in the

00:02:54.470 --> 00:02:59.560
MCU, and the Valkyries themselves weren't
exactly household names until Tessa Thompson's

00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:04.470
portrayal of the last surviving member of
Asgard's elite all-female fighting force in

00:03:04.470 --> 00:03:06.870
2017's Thor: Ragnarok.

00:03:06.870 --> 00:03:11.200
But among comics fans, Foster has picked up
a sizable fan base thanks to her time holding

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:15.840
down the mantle of Thor, and those fans should
be thrilled to see her back in action.

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:20.189
We'll see just how hard Mighty Marvel hits
the sweet spot when the first issue of Jane

00:03:20.189 --> 00:03:23.860
Foster: Valkyrie hits stands in July 2019.

